# nr-relay-scaffold: what the wiring applies (nothing here was compiled: cargo was not run)

New crate native/core/crates/mixdog-relay (complete: Cargo.toml, src/{lib,main,config,ids,close_codes,rate_limit,js,logline}.rs,
the area folders src/<area>/mod.rs (empty), src/server/mod.rs and src/tools/*.rs (stubs), src/bin/relay_twin_host.rs, tests/twin/main.rs,
tests/core_units.rs, tests/ledger/nr-relay-scaffold.json). Binary target `mixdog-relay` (src/main.rs). Its Cargo.toml fixes every
dependency the later tasks of the relay track use, so none of them edits it. Every third-party crate named is a `workspace = true`
entry that exists, except `pem = "3.0.6"`, which carries its version directly because the workspace has no `pem` entry (pem 3.0.6 is
already in Cargo.lock).

## 1. native/core/Cargo.toml (hot file)

Header comment, line 2: the text "one [[bin]] `mixdogd` in `mixdog-cli`" becomes
"one [[bin]] `mixdogd` in `mixdog-cli` and the relay server `mixdog-relay`, deployed alone on the relay host".

In `[workspace] members`, after the line `    "crates/mixdog-askpass",`:

    "crates/mixdog-relay",

In `[workspace.dependencies]`, after the line `mixdog-askpass = { path = "crates/mixdog-askpass" }`:

    mixdog-relay = { path = "crates/mixdog-relay" }

(The crate's own Cargo.toml does not use that entry.)

## 2. Cargo.lock and mixdog-workspace-hack (hot files)

Run `cargo update --workspace --offline`, then `cargo hakari generate`. The lock gains the package `mixdog-relay` and, through the
p256 features `ecdsa`, `pkcs8`, `pem` (added in the crate's Cargo.toml on top of the workspace entry), `pem-rfc7468` 0.7.0, which is in the
cargo cache. tokio-tungstenite uses `rustls-tls-native-roots` (as mixdog-ai does), not the webpki-roots feature.

## 3. SERVICE_PENDING (compose_flip.rs)

No protocol method and no service is added by this task: no name changes.

## 4. Verify

    cargo build -p mixdog-relay --offline
    cargo nextest run -p mixdog-relay --features test-support --offline
    cargo clippy -p mixdog-relay --all-targets --features test-support --offline -- -D warnings
